{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AVF1m2NgGpMfVXo3Zei26J","type":"tool_result","content":"<stdin>:3: DeprecationWarning: datetime.datetime.utcnow() is deprecated and scheduled for removal in a future version. Use timezone-aware objects to represent datetimes in UTC: datetime.datetime.now(datetime.UTC).\n68:\\paragraph{Semi-supervised and debiased estimation.} The control-variate form of PPI has antecedents in semi-supervised mean estimation \\citep{Zhang2016SemisupervisedIG} and in semiparametrically efficient semi-supervised learning \\citep{Xu2025AUF}, where e\n70:\\paragraph{Calibration.} Isotonic and binned maps from scores to outcome probabilities are standard calibration tools \\citep{Zadrozny2002TransformingCS,Niculescu-Mizil2005PredictingGP}. Here they estimate $\\E[Y\\mid \\Yhat]$ for use as a control variate, not \n120:\\paragraph{Pools and draws.} The sealed evaluation uses four real pools, each with $n=500$ labeled and $N=20000$ unlabeled records: California census income, census private-insurance indicator, a census education-related quantity (all with model prediction\n124:\\paragraph{Design-space contrast.} Before the sealed evaluation, three model variants were scored once each on separate search pools (galaxy morphology, Amazon deforestation, gene expression, protein disorder, plus synthetic regimes; 60 draws per family): \n136:Most of the gain over labeled-only inference is therefore already captured by PPI machinery; recalibration adds a small increment on top. Per family, the narrowing against PPI++ is 0.0287 for census income, 0.0018 for census insurance, 0.0023 for census ed\n158:plankton & 0.0359 & 3.5\\% & 0.0000 & 0.0000 & 0.0359 \\\\\n174:\\emph{Where the observed gain exceeds the ceiling.} In four of five families the observed narrowing is larger than the ceiling (Table~\\ref{tab:final}). The plankton pool is the clearest case: both $Y$ and $\\Yhat$ are binary, $\\E[Y\\mid\\Yhat]$ is therefore e\n203:The recalibrated variant is largest on the synthetic family (0.0757) and gene expression (0.0290), and smallest on galaxy morphology (0.0035). % @evidence[[source_evidence/search_metrics/recalibrated_metrics.json]]\n204:The stacked variant tracks it on the synthetic family (0.0707) and gene expression (0.0278) but is smaller on deforestation and protein disorder; the smooth label-free basis is close to PPI++ on the synthetic family (0.0034), where the nonlinearity is the \n218:\\paragraph{What it does not support.} The evidence does not show that the narrowing is free: coverage point estimates are 0.934 pooled and 0.91 for the lowest family, below 0.95, and the baselines' coverage is unknown. The observed gain exceeds the ceiling\n277:Search pools: galaxy morphology (Galaxy Zoo-type crowd labels, \\citealt{Willett2013GalaxyZ2}; $n=300$, $N=5000$), Amazon deforestation ($n=100$, $N=1000$), gene expression ($n=500$, $N=10000$), protein disorder ($n=300$, $N=5000$), and synthetic regimes, 6\n293:plankton (binary $\\Yhat$) & 0.7004 & 0.7004 & 0.0000 & 0.841 \\\\","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9a95e96-2cf4-41d1-b724-cfa8cc26020e","uuid":"a8f3d0e7-36c2-4b60-877b-50185a086b6b","timestamp":"2026-11-11T12:08:18.718Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"<stdin>:3: DeprecationWarning: datetime.datetime.utcnow() is deprecated and scheduled for removal in a future version. Use timezone-aware objects to represent datetimes in UTC: datetime.datetime.now(datetime.UTC).\n68:\\paragraph{Semi-supervised and debiased estimation.} The control-variate form of PPI has antecedents in semi-supervised mean estimation \\citep{Zhang2016SemisupervisedIG} and in semiparametrically efficient semi-supervised learning \\citep{Xu2025AUF}, where e\n70:\\paragraph{Calibration.} Isotonic and binned maps from scores to outcome probabilities are standard calibration tools \\citep{Zadrozny2002TransformingCS,Niculescu-Mizil2005PredictingGP}. Here they estimate $\\E[Y\\mid \\Yhat]$